<li>
<p>
Create a graph of your data. You need a title, axis titles, and a key as you use a different color for each organism
</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
List the factors that contributed to the loss of biodiversity of the forest community in order of how frequently they occurred over the 15 years, beginning with the most frequent and ending with the least
</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
Which event had the most devastating immediate consequence to a population? Which event caused a population to decline the most over the long term?
</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
Based on the game’s results, calculate the percent change in each species’ population in the ecosystem.
</p>
<me>\text{Percent Change} = [\frac{\text{(Final Population – Initial Population)}}{\text{Initial Population}}]x100%</me>
